; LEVER-1 (2026-08-29) -- the sign Talon asked for, and the surface his warning lands on.
;
;   "There needs to be a sign at least that it will reset the bubble counter and a warning ...
;    because I would be upset if I spent hours collecting all the bubbles and then someone reset
;    my progress."
;
; FOUR faces, not one. This lever stands free in the open 1.5 m east of the plinth, so it is
; walked up to from every direction; the hub's own plinth signs get away with two because a
; plinth has a front. One plate per face of the base, 12 mm proud of it, so the lever says what
; it does from wherever a player arrives.
;
; NOT BILLBOARDED, and the mode is written out explicitly below rather than left to the engine
; default so the intent is legible in the file: UI-1 removed five camera-facing SectionLabels
; from this very level on 2026-08-28 because Talon objected to hover UI, and adding one back in
; the same week would be undoing his note with his other note. Godot may strip an explicit
; default on an editor re-save, so the test guarding this asserts the ABSENCE of any ENABLED
; billboard mode -- with the five in scenes/dev/ArcheryLab.tscn as its positive control --
; rather than the presence of the line below.
;
; TEXT is authored here AND written at runtime by BubbleResetLever.ApplySigns. The scene copy is
; what the editor and the packed-scene test see; the runtime copy is what swaps in the warning
; and the live tally. They must say the same idle words -- BubbleResetLever.SignIdleText is the
; source and a unit test pins the two together.
;
; SIZE is measured, not guessed. font_size 96 x pixel_size 0.00035 = 0.0336 m/em, so a cap is
; ~23 mm and the longest line (18 characters) is ~0.41 m -- inside the 0.5 m narrow face. At the
; 1.6 m PressRadius a player actually stands at, a 23 mm cap subtends ~50 arcmin, against the
; ~20 arcmin that reads as comfortable and the ~5 arcmin acuity limit. See the LEVER-1 report
; for the rendered measurement.
;
; UNSHADED (Label3D's default) is deliberate and is the reason there is no light here: the sign
; has to be readable in this hub at night, and BT-8's "the display is the only light in the
; scene it ships with" is still true -- an unshaded label emits nothing and lights nothing.

[node name="Signs" type="Node3D" parent="."]

